"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n5le02ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Registering data and information into databases won't be a flawless activity as errors are easy to commit. Two are the most common slips that we can commit when it comes to registering important pieces of information in databases or systems. Whenever we have got to transfer data from one main source, such as a customer, to a database, there is a high chance of us committing transcription errors. These will not occur unless we misread or mishear elements like numbers, foreign names or addresses introducing wrong pieces of information into the system. Another common type of error is the transposition error in which we unintentionally change similar pieces of information in numbers or words to other similar values without noticing it. </div>"}, {"time": "47200", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Different built-in tools are going to help users prevent other types of mistakes. This is the case of the field level validation, which avoids the errors caused by the human interaction with the system as it portrays a series of different pre-established fields for the user to completely fill in a given order and way. If the data is not correct, it won't be registered in the database; in fact, the user will be alerted about the error. For example, email addresses that lack the \u201c@\u201d symbol are going to be rejected.</div>"}, {"time": "79300", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Finally, the form level validation is going to ensure that the user fills all the <i>de rigueur</i> data and that all special requirements are met before the data is submitted. This validation has got to be performed once the form is completely filled in order to proceed with a whole validation of the input that was introduced. Furthermore, this type of validation will not let the user register the form if there's missing information on a required field marked with a \u201c*\u201d symbol.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le02ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}